# Reducing the empty rule b on X leads to a unit reduction d → b and back to
# the same state, with nothing consumed: the generated parser pushed forever
# on "x" and "xc". A loop through reductions of any length is rejected.
# error: empty_unit_reduction_loop.grammar:21:
# error: leads back to the same state
@lexer
tokens
    x
    c
    eof
    err
'x'   → x
'c'   → c
.     → err

@parser
top! = a
a = d a C → (a 2)
  | X
d = b → (d)
b = <
